            "id": "19470632",
            "user": "WikiHowUser20220204205835",
            "timestamp": "09:44, 19 January 2016",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(12,033 bytes)",
            "change": 10,
            "summary": "(RCP reverted edits by Micheal Regacho (talk) to  revision #19399670 by RelatedWikihowsBot)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "revert",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Check for hazards inside your home and begin to fix them. There are a number of specific hazards in your home that you can deal with before an earthquake occurs.[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 1 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Create a Disaster Preparedness Plan. Know what you and your family are going to do before the earthquake happens. Form your plan together and go over it on a regular basis.[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 2 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*Decide on a rallying point for your family for after the earthquake. It should be away from buildings. Go over what your family should do in the event that not everyone makes it to the rallying point. If you have civil defence safety meeting points, be sure that every member of the family knows the location of the one closest to home, school, and work. Identify an out-of-area contact person that your family can call and get in touch with one another.",
                    "#[[Pack an Emergency Kit for the House|Prepare disaster supplies]] in advance. The following items are important to have readily available in your home, situated in a central location:[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 3 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*Purchase and use \"[[Use a Glowstick|glow sticks]]\". Keep candles handy as well, but be careful. You may be dealing with ruptured gas lines or flammable material spills.",
                    "#Work with your community to be prepared. If there aren't civic groups present in your area focused on earthquake preparedness, work on putting one together. The first step in keeping everyone safe is education.[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 4 Version 2.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Check for hazards inside your home and begin to fix them. There are a number of specific hazards in your home that you can deal with before an earthquake occurs.[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 1 Version 2.|center]]",
                    "#Create a Disaster Preparedness Plan. Know what you and your family are going to do before the earthquake happens. Form your plan together and go over it on a regular basis.[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 2 Version 2.|center]]",
                    "#*Decide on a rallying point for your family for after the earthquake. It should be away from buildings. Go over what your family should do in the event that not everyone makes it to the rallying point. If you have civil deffence safety meeting points, be sure that every member of the family knows the location of the one closest to home, school, and work. Identify an out-of-area contact person that your family can call and get in touch with one another.",
                    "#[[Pack an Emergency Kit for the House|Prepare disaster supplies]] in advance. The following items are important to have readily available in your home, situated in a central location:[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 3 Version 2.|center]]",
                    "#*Purchase and use \"[[Use a Glow stick|glow sticks]]\". Keep candles handy as well, but be careful. You may be dealing with ruptured gas lines or flammable material spills.",
                    "#Work with your community to be prepared. If there aren't civic groups present in your area focused on earthquake preparedness, work on putting one together. The first step in keeping everyone safe is education.[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 4 Version 2.|center]]"
                ]
            }
