            "id": "13455421",
            "user": "Wikivisual",
            "timestamp": "15:20, 29 April 2014",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(12,944 bytes)",
            "change": 33,
            "summary": "(Enlarging and centering Steps photos)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "reverted",
            "contribution_type": "addition",
            "reverted_by": "Hailey",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Check for hazards inside your home and begin to fix them. There are a number of specific hazards in your home that you can deal with before an earthquake occurs.<br><br>[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 1 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Create a Disaster Preparedness Plan. Know what you and your family are going to do before the earthquake happens. Form your plan together and go over it on a regular basis.<br><br>[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 2 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#[[Pack an Emergency Kit for the House|Prepare disaster supplies]] in advance. The following items are important to have readily available in your home, situated in a central location:<br><br>[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 3 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Work with your community to be prepared. If there aren't civic groups present in your area focused on earthquake preparedness, work on putting one together. The first step in keeping everyone safe is education.<br><br>[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 4 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    ""
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Check for hazards inside your home and begin to fix them. There are a number of specific hazards in your home that you can deal with before an earthquake occurs.[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 1 Version 2.jpg|center|300px]]",
                    "#Create a Disaster Preparedness Plan. Know what you and your family are going to do before the earthquake happens. Form your plan together and go over it on a regular basis.[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 2 Version 2.jpg|center|300px]]",
                    "#[[Pack an Emergency Kit for the House|Prepare disaster supplies]] in advance. The following items are important to have readily available in your home, situated in a central location:[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 3 Version 2.jpg|center|300px]]",
                    "#Work with your community to be prepared. If there aren't civic groups present in your area focused on earthquake preparedness, work on putting one together. The first step in keeping everyone safe is education.[[Image:Prepare for an Earthquake Step 4 Version 2.jpg|center|300px]]"
                ]
            }
        },
