                "removed": [
                    "{{nointroimg}}{{fa}}An earthquake is a very destructive natural disaster; particularly in the Pacific Rim region. In fact, scientists now believe that California is long overdue for a massive earthquake along the San Andreas fault, with a magnitude of up to 8.0.<ref>Rong-Gong Lin Il, Study shakes up scientists' view of San Andreas earthquake risk, http://www.latimes.com/news/local/la-me-earthquake-fault-20100821,0,946323.story?track=rss</ref>",
                    "",
                    "After an earthquake, your home may be a mess and you might be left without a water supply and energy. There are several things you can do to prepare for an earthquake before it happens, to minimize the damage and potential for injury in and around your home.",
                    "{{reflist}}"
                ]
            }
        },
