            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#*Heavy pictures, light fixtures, and [[Build a Mirror|mirrors]] should be hung away from beds, couches, and anywhere that someone might sit. Conventional picture hooks will not hold pictures during an earthquake but they are easy to fix - simply push the hook closed, or use a filler material to fill the gap between the hook and its backing. Other alternatives include buying special art hooks, and ensuring that heavy painting have adequate, strong hooks and strong cord."
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#*Heavy pictures, light fixtures, and [[Build a Mirror|mirrors]] should be hung away from beds, couches, and anywhere that someone might sit. Conventional picture hooks will notchold pictures during an earthquake but they are easy to fix - simply push the hook closed, or use a filler material to fill the gap between the hook and its backing. Other alternatives include buying special art hooks, and ensuring that heavy painting have adequate, strong hooks and strong cord."
                ]
            }
